        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.239,
            0.293,
            0.261
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.264,
            0.773,
            0.284
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Find out the units digit in the value of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2^{224} \\div 4^{32} ?"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " [Hint: "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 = 2 ^ { 2 } ]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.294,
            0.848,
            0.333
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. There are 5 bottles in a container. Every day, a new container is brought in. How many bottles would be there after 40 days?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.342,
            0.847,
            0.405
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Write the given number as the product of two or more powers in three different ways. The powers can be any integers. (i) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 4 ^ { 3 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (ii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 9 2 ^ { 8 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (iii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 2 ^ { - 5 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.409,
            0.845,
            0.448
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Examine each statement below and find out if it is ‘Always True’, ‘Only Sometimes True’, or ‘Never True’. Explain your reasoning."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.189,
            0.452,
            0.633,
            0.471
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Cube numbers are also square numbers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.183,
            0.471,
            0.631,
            0.489
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Fourth powers are also square numbers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.489,
            0.846,
            0.525
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) The fifth power of a number is divisible by the cube of that number."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.525,
            0.743,
            0.544
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) The product of two cube numbers is a cube number."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.183,
            0.544,
            0.836,
            0.564
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(v) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "q ^ { 4 6 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is both a 4th power and a 6th power (q is a prime number)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.568,
            0.665,
            0.648
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Simplify and write these in the exponential form. (i) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 ^ { - 2 } \\times 1 0 ^ { - 5 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (ii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5 ^ { 7 } \\div 5 ^ { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (iii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "9 ^ { -   7 } \\div 9 ^ { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (iv) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( 1 3 ^ { -   2 } ) ^ { -   3 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (v) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "m ^ { 5 } n ^ { 1 2 } ( m n ) ^ { 9 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.652,
            0.637,
            0.716
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. If "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 2 ^ { 2 } = 1 4 4"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " what is (i) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( 1 . 2 ) ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (ii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( 0 . 1 2 ) ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (iii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( 0 . 0 1 2 ) ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (iv) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 2 0 ^ { 2 }"
            }
          ]
        },
